    {
      "name": "emma-story1-ride",
      "title": "A ride to warn Joseph",
      "description": "Family history tells how Emma learned that men were plotting to steal the gold plates, took a spare horse, and rode more than an hour to warn Joseph so he could move the record to safety. Lucy Mack Smith told the story years afterward. It is not a moment anyone stood by to witness. It is a true family memory of a young wife who was watchful, practical, and willing to go herself.",
      "alt": "Emma Smith at twenty three, wearing a long blue dress, rides sidesaddle at a gallop on a brown horse up a leaf covered slope in autumn, leaning forward with both hands on the reins and her eyes on the path ahead.",
      "page": "history/emma-elect-lady.html",
      "slotId": "picture-emma-story1-ride",
      "source": "https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/liahona/2021/03/emma-protected-scripture?lang=eng",
