    {
      "name": "emma-story2-hymnal",
      "title": "The finished hymnbook",
      "description": "The little book in her hands is the finished work: A Collection of Sacred Hymns, the selection of sacred hymns she was charged to make in Doctrine and Covenants 25. The edition is dated 1835, and the printed books reached the Saints early in 1836. What she holds here is the completed collection, ninety hymns she chose, small enough to carry into any home or meeting room where the Saints sang together.",
      "alt": "Emma Smith at thirty one, wearing a brown dress, stands by a window holding a small bound book in both hands and looking down at it.",
