    {
      "name": "emma-story3-quincy",
      "title": "Emma in Quincy",
      "description": "This portrait belongs to Emma's Quincy season, the weeks after the crossing. It is not the crossing itself. It is the woman who wrote from Quincy on March 7, 1839, that she was still living and still willing. Her hands rest in her lap, work worn and uninjured: the hands that had carried her children over the ice and then picked up a pen.",
      "alt": "Emma Smith at thirty four, wearing a gray dress, sits by a window with her hands folded in her lap and her gaze lowered.",
      "page": "history/emma-winter-crossing.html",
