    {
      "name": "emma-story4-hospitality",
      "title": "An open door",
      "description": "Across her Nauvoo years, Emma opened her home again and again to the sick, the orphaned, and the homeless. It was a practice, not one day's kindness: a door held open by the woman of the house, with the welcome ready before anyone is seen. She stands in her doorway with one hand resting on the open door, ready for whoever needed shelter next.",
      "alt": "Emma Smith at thirty eight, wearing a dark green dress, stands in the open doorway of her home with one hand resting on the door.",
      "page": "history/emma-relief-society.html",
      "slotId": "picture-emma-story4-hospitality",
      "source": "https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/history/topics/female-relief-society-of-nauvoo?lang=eng",
