    {
      "name": "emma-story5-testimony",
      "title": "Her testimony",
      "description": "Near the end of her life, Emma spoke with her son Joseph III about the Book of Mormon, and after her death his account of their conversation was published. As her son Joseph III recorded it, her words were plain: 'My belief is that the Book of Mormon is of divine authenticity—I have not the slightest doubt of it.' That testimony was not new at seventy four. It was the same witness she had carried since Harmony, kept to the end of her life.",
      "alt": "Emma Smith at seventy four, wearing a dark gray dress, sits speaking, one hand raised in conversation, her gaze toward the one she is speaking with.",
      "page": "history/emma-last-testimony.html",
      "slotId": "picture-emma-story5-testimony",
      "source": "https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/ensign/1992/08/my-great-great-grandmother-emma-hale-smith?lang=eng",
